/-!
# The facet presentation ring of a Delzant polytope

Let `Δ = {x | c j ≤ ⟨x, u j⟩ for every j}` be the polyhedron of a facet presentation with inward
normals `u : ι → N` in a lattice `N` and support constants `c : ι → ℝ`
(`TauCeti.Toric.facetPolyhedron i u c`). When `Δ` is a Delzant polytope, the integral cohomology
ring of the symplectic toric manifold `M_Δ` it determines has a presentation by generators and
relations read off from `Δ`, one generator `D j` for each facet: `D j` is the class of the
divisor `μ⁻¹(F j)` over the facet `F j`. This file defines the ring of that presentation, over an
arbitrary commutative ring `k` of coefficients, and computes it for the standard simplex. The
comparison with the cohomology of the toric manifold is not made here.

A finite set `s` of facets is a *nonface* (`TauCeti.Toric.IsNonface`) when no point of `Δ` lies on
all of the facets in `s`, that is, when the corresponding divisors have empty intersection. The
**Stanley–Reisner ideal** (`TauCeti.Toric.stanleyReisnerIdeal`) is generated by the monomials
`∏_{j ∈ s} D j` of the nonfaces `s`; for a Delzant polytope, the quotient of `k[D j | j ∈ ι]` by
it is the presentation of the equivariant cohomology ring `H_T^*(M_Δ; k)`. Each additive map
`φ : N →+ k`, a weight of the torus with coefficients in `k`, gives the **linear relation**
`∑ j, φ (u j) D j` (`TauCeti.Toric.linearRelation`), the image of the equivariant class `φ` of
the base `BT`, and these span the **linear relation ideal**
(`TauCeti.Toric.linearRelationIdeal`). The quotient by both ideals (`TauCeti.Toric.FacetRing`) is
the ring which, by the theorem of Danilov and Jurkiewicz, presents the ordinary cohomology ring
`H^*(M_Δ; k)` of a Delzant polytope.

The support constants determine a class `∑ j, c j D j` (`TauCeti.Toric.supportClass`) with real
coefficients. In the convention of the reversed action and inward normals, the cohomology class of
the reduced symplectic form corresponds to `-2π ∑ j, c j D j`. Translating `Δ` by `y` replaces
`c j` by `c j + ⟨y, u j⟩`; this changes neither the nonfaces (`TauCeti.Toric.isNonface_add_iff`) nor
therefore the ideals, and changes the class by the linear relation of the weight `⟨y, i ·⟩`, so
the class in the facet ring is invariant under translation
(`TauCeti.Toric.mk_supportClass_add`), as `[ω]` is under shifting the moment map.

For the standard simplex of size `a > 0` (`TauCeti.Toric.simplexNormal κ`,
`TauCeti.Toric.simplexSupport a`), the moment polytope of `ℂPⁿ` with `n = #κ`, the only nonface
is the set of all `n + 1` facets (`TauCeti.Toric.isNonface_simplex_iff`), and the linear relations
identify all the generators. So the facet ring is the truncated polynomial ring

`k[D] ⧸ (∏ o, D o, D (some m) - D none) ≃ k[x] ⧸ (x ^ (n + 1))`,

each generator going to `x` (`TauCeti.Toric.facetRingSimplexEquiv`), the cohomology ring of `ℂPⁿ`
with `x` the hyperplane class. The class `-∑ j, c j D j` goes to `a x`
(`TauCeti.Toric.facetRingSimplexEquiv_mk_neg_supportClass`), so `-2π ∑ j, c j D j` goes to
`2π a x`. For `n = 1` the simplex is the interval `[0, a]`, `M_Δ` is the sphere, and `x` is the
positive point class: the class `-2π ∑ j, c j D j` is `2π a` times the point class.

## Main definitions

* `TauCeti.Toric.IsNonface i u c s`: no point of the polyhedron lies on all the facets in `s`.
* `TauCeti.Toric.stanleyReisnerIdeal i u c k`: the ideal of the monomials of the nonfaces.
* `TauCeti.Toric.linearRelationIdeal u k`: the ideal of the linear relations `∑ j, φ (u j) D j`.
* `TauCeti.Toric.FacetRing i u c k`: the quotient of `k[D j | j ∈ ι]` by both ideals.
* `TauCeti.Toric.supportClass c`: the class `∑ j, c j D j`.
* `TauCeti.Toric.facetRingSimplexEquiv`: the facet ring of the simplex is `k[x] ⧸ (x ^ (n + 1))`.

## Main results

* `TauCeti.Toric.stanleyReisnerIdeal_add`, `TauCeti.Toric.facetIdeal_add`: translating the
  polyhedron does not change the ideals.
* `TauCeti.Toric.mk_supportClass_add`: translating the polyhedron does not change the class of
  `∑ j, c j D j` in the facet ring.
* `TauCeti.Toric.isNonface_simplex_iff`: the only nonface of the simplex is the set of all facets.
* `TauCeti.Toric.facetRingSimplexEquiv_mk_neg_supportClass`: for the simplex of size `a`, the class
  `-∑ j, c j D j` is `a x`.

## References

* A. Cannas da Silva, *Lectures on Symplectic Geometry*, Lecture Notes in Mathematics 1764,
  Springer, 2001, Sections 28–29.
* V. Guillemin, *Moment Maps and Combinatorial Invariants of Hamiltonian `T^n`-spaces*,
  Birkhäuser, 1994, Chapter 1 and Appendix 2 (the cohomology ring of a toric manifold).
* V. I. Danilov, *The geometry of toric varieties*, Russian Math. Surveys 33 (1978), 97–154,
  Theorem 10.8 (the ring presentation).
* W. Fulton, *Introduction to Toric Varieties*, Annals of Mathematics Studies 131, Princeton
  University Press, 1993, Section 5.2.
-/

public section

noncomputable section

open Set MvPolynomial

namespace TauCeti.Toric

variable {ι N V : Type*} [AddCommGroup N] [NormedAddCommGroup V] [NormedSpace ℝ V]
  (i : N →+ V) (u : ι → N) (c : ι → ℝ) (k : Type*) [CommRing k]

/-- A finite set `s` of facets is a *nonface* of the facet presentation when no point of the
polyhedron lies on all of the facets in `s`. -/
def IsNonface (s : Finset ι) : Prop :=
  ∀ x ∈ facetPolyhedron i u c, ¬(s : Set ι) ⊆ activeSet (facetPairing i u) c x

/-- The **Stanley–Reisner ideal** of a facet presentation: the ideal of `k[D j | j ∈ ι]`
generated by the monomials `∏_{j ∈ s} D j` of the nonfaces `s`. -/
def stanleyReisnerIdeal : Ideal (MvPolynomial ι k) :=
  Ideal.span ((fun s : Finset ι ↦ ∏ j ∈ s, X j) '' {s | IsNonface i u c s})

variable [Fintype ι]

/-- The **linear relation** `∑ j, φ (u j) D j` of a weight `φ : N →+ k`. -/
def linearRelation (φ : N →+ k) : MvPolynomial ι k :=
  ∑ j, C (φ (u j)) * X j

/-- The ideal of `k[D j | j ∈ ι]` spanned by the linear relations `∑ j, φ (u j) D j` of all the
weights `φ : N →+ k`. -/
def linearRelationIdeal : Ideal (MvPolynomial ι k) :=
  Ideal.span (range (linearRelation u k))

/-- The ideal of the facet presentation: the Stanley–Reisner ideal together with the linear
relations. -/
def facetIdeal : Ideal (MvPolynomial ι k) :=
  stanleyReisnerIdeal i u c k ⊔ linearRelationIdeal u k

/-- The **facet presentation ring** `k[D j | j ∈ ι] ⧸ (I_SR + J)` of a facet presentation, with
one generator for each facet, the Stanley–Reisner relations of the nonfaces and the linear
relations of the weights. For a Delzant polytope, the theorem of Danilov and Jurkiewicz identifies
it with the cohomology ring of the symplectic toric manifold of the polytope. -/
abbrev FacetRing : Type _ :=
  MvPolynomial ι k ⧸ facetIdeal i u c k

/-- The class `∑ j, c j D j` of the support constants. In the convention of the reversed action
and inward normals, `-2π` times it corresponds to the class of the reduced symplectic form. -/
def supportClass : MvPolynomial ι ℝ :=
  ∑ j, C (c j) * X j

omit [Fintype ι] in
variable {i u c} in
theorem isNonface_def {s : Finset ι} :
    IsNonface i u c s ↔
      ∀ x ∈ facetPolyhedron i u c, ¬(s : Set ι) ⊆ activeSet (facetPairing i u) c x :=
  Iff.rfl

omit [Fintype ι] in
theorem stanleyReisnerIdeal_def :
    stanleyReisnerIdeal i u c k =
      Ideal.span ((fun s : Finset ι ↦ ∏ j ∈ s, X j) '' {s | IsNonface i u c s}) :=
  (rfl)

theorem linearRelation_def (φ : N →+ k) : linearRelation u k φ = ∑ j, C (φ (u j)) * X j :=
  (rfl)

theorem linearRelationIdeal_def :
    linearRelationIdeal u k = Ideal.span (range (linearRelation u k)) :=
  (rfl)

theorem facetIdeal_def :
    facetIdeal i u c k = stanleyReisnerIdeal i u c k ⊔ linearRelationIdeal u k :=
  (rfl)

theorem supportClass_def : supportClass c = ∑ j, C (c j) * X j :=
  (rfl)

/-- An ideal contains the ideal of the facet presentation exactly when it contains both the
Stanley–Reisner ideal and the linear relations. -/
theorem facetIdeal_le_iff {J : Ideal (MvPolynomial ι k)} :
    facetIdeal i u c k ≤ J ↔ stanleyReisnerIdeal i u c k ≤ J ∧ linearRelationIdeal u k ≤ J :=
  sup_le_iff

omit [Fintype ι] in
/-- An ideal contains the Stanley–Reisner ideal exactly when it contains the monomial of every
nonface. -/
theorem stanleyReisnerIdeal_le_iff {J : Ideal (MvPolynomial ι k)} :
    stanleyReisnerIdeal i u c k ≤ J ↔ ∀ s, IsNonface i u c s → ∏ j ∈ s, X j ∈ J := by
  simp [stanleyReisnerIdeal_def, Ideal.span_le, Set.subset_def]

/-- An ideal contains the linear relations exactly when it contains the linear relation of every
weight. -/
theorem linearRelationIdeal_le_iff {J : Ideal (MvPolynomial ι k)} :
    linearRelationIdeal u k ≤ J ↔ ∀ φ, linearRelation u k φ ∈ J := by
  simp [linearRelationIdeal_def, Ideal.span_le, Set.range_subset_iff]

@[simp]
theorem linearRelation_mem_linearRelationIdeal (φ : N →+ k) :
    linearRelation u k φ ∈ linearRelationIdeal u k :=
  Ideal.subset_span ⟨φ, rfl⟩

theorem linearRelationIdeal_le_facetIdeal : linearRelationIdeal u k ≤ facetIdeal i u c k :=
  le_sup_right

theorem stanleyReisnerIdeal_le_facetIdeal : stanleyReisnerIdeal i u c k ≤ facetIdeal i u c k :=
  le_sup_left

variable {i u c k}

omit [Fintype ι] in
/-- The monomial of a nonface lies in the Stanley–Reisner ideal. -/
theorem IsNonface.prod_mem_stanleyReisnerIdeal {s : Finset ι} (hs : IsNonface i u c s) :
    ∏ j ∈ s, X j ∈ stanleyReisnerIdeal i u c k :=
  Ideal.subset_span ⟨s, hs, rfl⟩

omit [Fintype ι] in
/-- A set of facets containing a nonface is a nonface. -/
theorem IsNonface.mono {s t : Finset ι} (hs : IsNonface i u c s) (hst : s ⊆ t) :
    IsNonface i u c t :=
  fun x hx h ↦ hs x hx ((Finset.coe_subset.2 hst).trans h)

omit [Fintype ι] in
/-- The empty set of facets is a nonface exactly when the polyhedron is empty. -/
@[simp]
theorem isNonface_empty_iff : IsNonface i u c ∅ ↔ facetPolyhedron i u c = ∅ := by
  simp [IsNonface, eq_empty_iff_forall_notMem]

/-- The linear relation of the zero weight is zero. -/
@[simp]
theorem linearRelation_zero : linearRelation u k 0 = 0 := by
  simp [linearRelation]

/-- The linear relation of the sum of two weights is the sum of their linear relations. -/
@[simp]
theorem linearRelation_add (φ ψ : N →+ k) :
    linearRelation u k (φ + ψ) = linearRelation u k φ + linearRelation u k ψ := by
  simp [linearRelation, add_mul, Finset.sum_add_distrib]

/-- The linear relation of the negative of a weight is the negative of its linear relation. -/
@[simp]
theorem linearRelation_neg (φ : N →+ k) : linearRelation u k (-φ) = -linearRelation u k φ := by
  simp [linearRelation, neg_mul, Finset.sum_neg_distrib]

/-- The linear relation of the difference of two weights is the difference of their linear
relations. -/
@[simp]
theorem linearRelation_sub (φ ψ : N →+ k) :
    linearRelation u k (φ - ψ) = linearRelation u k φ - linearRelation u k ψ := by
  simp [sub_eq_add_neg]

/-! ### Translations -/

section Translation

variable (y : StrongDual ℝ V)

omit [Fintype ι] in
/-- **Translation preserves the nonfaces.** -/
@[simp]
theorem isNonface_add_iff {s : Finset ι} :
    IsNonface i u (fun j ↦ c j + y (i (u j))) s ↔ IsNonface i u c s := by
  simp only [IsNonface, facetPolyhedron_add, mem_vadd_set, vadd_eq_add, forall_exists_index,
    and_imp, forall_apply_eq_imp_iff₂, activeSet_add]

omit [Fintype ι] in
/-- Translating the polyhedron does not change the Stanley–Reisner ideal. -/
@[simp]
theorem stanleyReisnerIdeal_add :
    stanleyReisnerIdeal i u (fun j ↦ c j + y (i (u j))) k = stanleyReisnerIdeal i u c k := by
  simp only [stanleyReisnerIdeal_def, isNonface_add_iff]

/-- Translating the polyhedron does not change the ideal of the facet presentation. -/
@[simp]
theorem facetIdeal_add :
    facetIdeal i u (fun j ↦ c j + y (i (u j))) k = facetIdeal i u c k := by
  rw [facetIdeal_def, facetIdeal_def, stanleyReisnerIdeal_add]

/-- Translating the polyhedron by `y` changes the class `∑ j, c j D j` by the linear relation of
the weight `⟨y, i ·⟩`. -/
theorem supportClass_add :
    supportClass (fun j ↦ c j + y (i (u j))) =
      supportClass c + linearRelation u ℝ ((y : V →+ ℝ).comp i) := by
  simp [supportClass, linearRelation, add_mul, Finset.sum_add_distrib]

/-- **Translation invariance of the support class.** Translating the polyhedron does not change
the class of `∑ j, c j D j` in the facet presentation ring. -/
theorem mk_supportClass_add :
    Ideal.Quotient.mk (facetIdeal i u c ℝ) (supportClass fun j ↦ c j + y (i (u j))) =
      Ideal.Quotient.mk (facetIdeal i u c ℝ) (supportClass c) := by
  rw [supportClass_add, map_add, add_eq_left, Ideal.Quotient.eq_zero_iff_mem]
  exact linearRelationIdeal_le_facetIdeal i u c ℝ (linearRelation_mem_linearRelationIdeal u ℝ _)

end Translation

/-! ### The standard simplex -/

section Simplex

variable {κ : Type*} [DecidableEq κ] [Fintype κ] {a : ℝ}

/-- **The nonfaces of the simplex.** For `a > 0`, the only set of facets of the standard simplex
of size `a` with no common point is the set of all `#κ + 1` facets. -/
theorem isNonface_simplex_iff (ha : 0 < a) {s : Finset (Option κ)} :
    IsNonface ((Int.castAddHom ℝ).compLeft κ) (simplexNormal κ) (simplexSupport a) s ↔
      s = Finset.univ := by
  constructor
  · -- A proper subset of the facets meets at a vertex: at `0` if it omits the slanted facet,
    -- and at `a e k₀*` if it omits the coordinate facet `k₀`.
    intro hs
    by_contra hne
    obtain ⟨o, -, ho⟩ := Finset.exists_of_ssubset (Finset.ssubset_univ_iff.2 hne)
    cases o with
    | none =>
      refine hs 0 ((mem_extremePoints_facetPolyhedron_simplex_iff ha).2 (Or.inl rfl)).1
        fun o ho' ↦ ?_
      cases o with
      | none => exact absurd ho' ho
      | some k => simp
    | some k₀ =>
      let x : StrongDual ℝ (κ → ℝ) := a • ContinuousLinearMap.proj k₀
      have hx (k : κ) : x (Pi.single k 1) = if k = k₀ then a else 0 := by
        by_cases hk : k = k₀ <;> simp [x, hk]
      refine hs x ((mem_extremePoints_facetPolyhedron_simplex_iff ha).2 (Or.inr ⟨k₀, rfl⟩)).1
        fun o ho' ↦ ?_
      cases o with
      | none => simp [hx]
      | some k =>
        have hk : k ≠ k₀ := by rintro rfl; exact ho ho'
        rw [some_mem_activeSet_simplex_iff, hx]
        simp [hk]
  · -- On all the facets, the coordinates vanish and sum to `a`, which is impossible.
    rintro rfl x - hx
    have hnone : none ∈ activeSet (facetPairing ((Int.castAddHom ℝ).compLeft κ) (simplexNormal κ))
        (simplexSupport a) x :=
      hx (by simp)
    have hsome (k : κ) : x (Pi.single k 1) = 0 :=
      some_mem_activeSet_simplex_iff.1 (hx (by simp))
    rw [none_mem_activeSet_simplex_iff] at hnone
    simp only [hsome, Finset.sum_const_zero] at hnone
    exact ha.ne hnone

/-- The Stanley–Reisner ideal of the simplex is generated by the product of all the generators. -/
theorem stanleyReisnerIdeal_simplex (ha : 0 < a) :
    stanleyReisnerIdeal ((Int.castAddHom ℝ).compLeft κ) (simplexNormal κ) (simplexSupport a) k =
      Ideal.span {∏ o, X o} := by
  rw [stanleyReisnerIdeal_def]
  congr 1
  ext p
  simp [isNonface_simplex_iff ha]

/-- The weight `ℤ^κ → k` reading off the coordinate `k₀`. -/
private def coordinateWeight (k₀ : κ) : (κ → ℤ) →+ k :=
  (Int.castAddHom k).comp (Pi.evalAddMonoidHom (fun _ : κ ↦ ℤ) k₀)

/-- The linear relations of the simplex are spanned by the differences `D (some m) - D none`. -/
theorem linearRelationIdeal_simplex :
    linearRelationIdeal (simplexNormal κ) k =
      Ideal.span (range fun m : κ ↦ X (some m) - X none) := by
  apply le_antisymm
  · -- The linear relation of `φ` is `∑ m, φ (e m) (D (some m) - D none)`.
    rw [linearRelationIdeal_le_iff]
    intro φ
    have h : linearRelation (simplexNormal κ) k φ =
        ∑ m, C (φ (Pi.single m 1)) * (X (some m) - X none) := by
      have h1 : (1 : κ → ℤ) = ∑ m, Pi.single m 1 := (Finset.univ_sum_single 1).symm
      simp only [linearRelation, Fintype.sum_option, simplexNormal_none, simplexNormal_some,
        map_neg, h1, map_sum, mul_sub, Finset.sum_sub_distrib, neg_mul, Finset.sum_mul]
      ring
    rw [h]
    exact Submodule.sum_mem _ fun m _ ↦ Ideal.mul_mem_left _ _ (Ideal.subset_span ⟨m, rfl⟩)
  · -- The difference `D (some m) - D none` is the linear relation of the coordinate `m`.
    rw [Ideal.span_le]
    rintro _ ⟨m, rfl⟩
    have h : linearRelation (simplexNormal κ) k (coordinateWeight m) = X (some m) - X none := by
      simp [linearRelation, coordinateWeight, Fintype.sum_option, Pi.single_apply,
        sub_eq_neg_add]
    simpa only [h, SetLike.mem_coe] using
      linearRelation_mem_linearRelationIdeal (simplexNormal κ) k (coordinateWeight m)

variable (k) in
/-- In the facet ring of the normals of the simplex, for any support constants, every generator
`D o` is the generator `D none`. -/
theorem mk_X_simplex (c : Option κ → ℝ) (o : Option κ) :
    Ideal.Quotient.mk (facetIdeal ((Int.castAddHom ℝ).compLeft κ) (simplexNormal κ) c k) (X o) =
      Ideal.Quotient.mk (facetIdeal ((Int.castAddHom ℝ).compLeft κ) (simplexNormal κ) c k)
        (X none) := by
  cases o with
  | none => rfl
  | some m =>
    rw [Ideal.Quotient.eq]
    exact linearRelationIdeal_le_facetIdeal _ _ _ k
      (by rw [linearRelationIdeal_simplex]; exact Ideal.subset_span ⟨m, rfl⟩)

variable (k) in
/-- The map from `k[D o | o]` to `k[x] ⧸ (x ^ (#κ + 1))` sending every generator to `x`. -/
private def simplexGeneratorHom :
    MvPolynomial (Option κ) k →ₐ[k]
      Polynomial k ⧸ Ideal.span {(Polynomial.X : Polynomial k) ^ (Fintype.card κ + 1)} :=
  (Ideal.Quotient.mkₐ k _).comp (MvPolynomial.aeval fun _ ↦ Polynomial.X)

/-- The relations of the facet ring of the simplex hold in `k[x] ⧸ (x ^ (#κ + 1))`. -/
private theorem facetIdeal_simplex_le_ker (ha : 0 < a) :
    facetIdeal ((Int.castAddHom ℝ).compLeft κ) (simplexNormal κ) (simplexSupport a) k ≤
      RingHom.ker (simplexGeneratorHom k) := by
  rw [facetIdeal_le_iff, stanleyReisnerIdeal_simplex ha, linearRelationIdeal_simplex,
    Ideal.span_le, Ideal.span_le]
  constructor
  · rintro _ rfl
    simp only [SetLike.mem_coe, RingHom.mem_ker, map_prod, simplexGeneratorHom, AlgHom.comp_apply,
      aeval_X, Finset.prod_const, Finset.card_univ, Fintype.card_option]
    rw [Ideal.Quotient.mkₐ_eq_mk, ← map_pow, Ideal.Quotient.eq_zero_iff_mem]
    exact Ideal.mem_span_singleton_self _
  · rintro _ ⟨m, rfl⟩
    simp [simplexGeneratorHom]

/-- In the facet ring of the simplex, the generator `D none` has vanishing power
`D none ^ (#κ + 1)`, the monomial of the unique nonface. -/
private theorem mk_X_none_pow_simplex (ha : 0 < a) :
    Ideal.Quotient.mk (facetIdeal ((Int.castAddHom ℝ).compLeft κ) (simplexNormal κ)
      (simplexSupport a) k) (X none) ^ (Fintype.card κ + 1) = 0 := by
  -- Every generator is `D none`, so this power is the class of the monomial `∏ o, D o`.
  have hprod : Ideal.Quotient.mk (facetIdeal ((Int.castAddHom ℝ).compLeft κ) (simplexNormal κ)
      (simplexSupport a) k) (∏ o, X o) = Ideal.Quotient.mk _ (X none) ^ (Fintype.card κ + 1) := by
    simp only [map_prod, mk_X_simplex k (simplexSupport a), Finset.prod_const, Finset.card_univ,
      Fintype.card_option]
  rw [← hprod, Ideal.Quotient.eq_zero_iff_mem]
  exact stanleyReisnerIdeal_le_facetIdeal _ _ _ k
    ((isNonface_simplex_iff ha).2 rfl).prod_mem_stanleyReisnerIdeal

/-- The map of the facet ring of the simplex to `k[x] ⧸ (x ^ (#κ + 1))` sending every generator to
`x`. -/
private def facetRingSimplexHom (ha : 0 < a) :
    FacetRing ((Int.castAddHom ℝ).compLeft κ) (simplexNormal κ) (simplexSupport a) k →ₐ[k]
      Polynomial k ⧸ Ideal.span {(Polynomial.X : Polynomial k) ^ (Fintype.card κ + 1)} :=
  Ideal.Quotient.liftₐ _ (simplexGeneratorHom k) fun _ hp ↦
    RingHom.mem_ker.1 (facetIdeal_simplex_le_ker ha hp)

/-- `facetRingSimplexHom` on the class of a polynomial. -/
private theorem facetRingSimplexHom_mk (ha : 0 < a) (p : MvPolynomial (Option κ) k) :
    facetRingSimplexHom ha (Ideal.Quotient.mk _ p) = simplexGeneratorHom k p := by
  rw [← Ideal.Quotient.mkₐ_eq_mk k, ← AlgHom.comp_apply, facetRingSimplexHom,
    Ideal.Quotient.liftₐ_comp]

/-- The map of `k[x] ⧸ (x ^ (#κ + 1))` to the facet ring of the simplex sending `x` to `D none`. -/
private def simplexFacetRingHom (ha : 0 < a) :
    Polynomial k ⧸ Ideal.span {(Polynomial.X : Polynomial k) ^ (Fintype.card κ + 1)} →ₐ[k]
      FacetRing ((Int.castAddHom ℝ).compLeft κ) (simplexNormal κ) (simplexSupport a) k :=
  Ideal.Quotient.liftₐ _ ((Ideal.Quotient.mkₐ k _).comp (Polynomial.aeval (X none))) fun p hp ↦ by
    obtain ⟨q, rfl⟩ := Ideal.mem_span_singleton'.1 hp
    simp [Ideal.Quotient.mkₐ_eq_mk, mk_X_none_pow_simplex ha]

/-- `simplexFacetRingHom` on the class of a polynomial. -/
private theorem simplexFacetRingHom_mk (ha : 0 < a) (p : Polynomial k) :
    simplexFacetRingHom ha (Ideal.Quotient.mk _ p) =
      Ideal.Quotient.mk (facetIdeal ((Int.castAddHom ℝ).compLeft κ) (simplexNormal κ)
        (simplexSupport a) k) (Polynomial.aeval (X none) p) := by
  rw [← Ideal.Quotient.mkₐ_eq_mk k (Ideal.span _), ← AlgHom.comp_apply, simplexFacetRingHom,
    Ideal.Quotient.liftₐ_comp, AlgHom.comp_apply, Ideal.Quotient.mkₐ_eq_mk]

omit [DecidableEq κ] in
/-- `simplexGeneratorHom` sends every generator to `x`. -/
private theorem simplexGeneratorHom_X (o : Option κ) :
    simplexGeneratorHom k (X o) = Ideal.Quotient.mk _ Polynomial.X := by
  simp [simplexGeneratorHom, Ideal.Quotient.mkₐ_eq_mk]

/-- **The facet ring of the simplex.** For `a > 0` the facet presentation ring of the standard
simplex of size `a` in `ℝ^κ` is the truncated polynomial ring `k[x] ⧸ (x ^ (#κ + 1))`, the
cohomology ring of `ℂPⁿ`, each generator `D o` going to the hyperplane class `x`. -/
def facetRingSimplexEquiv (ha : 0 < a) :
    FacetRing ((Int.castAddHom ℝ).compLeft κ) (simplexNormal κ) (simplexSupport a) k ≃ₐ[k]
      Polynomial k ⧸ Ideal.span {(Polynomial.X : Polynomial k) ^ (Fintype.card κ + 1)} :=
  AlgEquiv.ofAlgHom (facetRingSimplexHom ha) (simplexFacetRingHom ha)
    (Ideal.Quotient.algHom_ext _ (Polynomial.algHom_ext (by
      simp [Ideal.Quotient.mkₐ_eq_mk, simplexFacetRingHom_mk, facetRingSimplexHom_mk,
        simplexGeneratorHom_X])))
    (Ideal.Quotient.algHom_ext _ (MvPolynomial.algHom_ext fun o ↦ by
      simp [Ideal.Quotient.mkₐ_eq_mk, simplexFacetRingHom_mk, facetRingSimplexHom_mk,
        simplexGeneratorHom_X, mk_X_simplex k (simplexSupport a) o]))

/-- The isomorphism `facetRingSimplexEquiv` sends every generator `D o` to `x`. -/
@[simp]
theorem facetRingSimplexEquiv_mk_X (ha : 0 < a) (o : Option κ) :
    facetRingSimplexEquiv (k := k) ha (Ideal.Quotient.mk _ (X o)) =
      Ideal.Quotient.mk (Ideal.span {(Polynomial.X : Polynomial k) ^ (Fintype.card κ + 1)})
        Polynomial.X := by
  rw [← AlgEquiv.coe_toAlgHom, facetRingSimplexEquiv, AlgEquiv.toAlgHom_ofAlgHom,
    facetRingSimplexHom_mk, simplexGeneratorHom_X]

/-- The inverse of `facetRingSimplexEquiv` sends `x` to the generator `D none`. -/
@[simp]
theorem facetRingSimplexEquiv_symm_mk_X (ha : 0 < a) :
    (facetRingSimplexEquiv (k := k) ha).symm
        (Ideal.Quotient.mk (Ideal.span {(Polynomial.X : Polynomial k) ^ (Fintype.card κ + 1)})
          Polynomial.X) =
      Ideal.Quotient.mk (facetIdeal ((Int.castAddHom ℝ).compLeft κ) (simplexNormal κ)
        (simplexSupport a) k) (X none) := by
  rw [AlgEquiv.symm_apply_eq, facetRingSimplexEquiv_mk_X]

omit [DecidableEq κ] in
/-- The class `∑ j, c j D j` of the simplex of size `a` is `-a D none`. -/
@[simp]
theorem supportClass_simplex : supportClass (simplexSupport (κ := κ) a) = -(C a * X none) := by
  simp [supportClass, Fintype.sum_option]

/-- **The support class of the simplex.** For the simplex of size `a > 0`, the class
`-∑ j, c j D j` is `a x` in `ℝ[x] ⧸ (x ^ (#κ + 1))`. So the class `-2π ∑ j, c j D j`, which
corresponds to the reduced symplectic form of `ℂPⁿ`, is `2π a` times the hyperplane class; for
`#κ = 1` this is the point class of the sphere. -/
theorem facetRingSimplexEquiv_mk_neg_supportClass (ha : 0 < a) :
    facetRingSimplexEquiv ha (Ideal.Quotient.mk _ (-supportClass (simplexSupport (κ := κ) a))) =
      a • Ideal.Quotient.mk (Ideal.span {(Polynomial.X : Polynomial ℝ) ^ (Fintype.card κ + 1)})
        Polynomial.X := by
  -- `-∑ j, c j D j` is `a • D none`; the quotient map is `ℝ`-linear as `mkₐ`, so the scalar
  -- comes out through both maps.
  rw [supportClass_simplex, neg_neg, C_mul', ← Ideal.Quotient.mkₐ_eq_mk ℝ, map_smul, map_smul]
  simp

end Simplex

